---
/*
 * DocKitty carrier: Sidebar (the sixth carrier, ADR-0063; FR-004, NFR-005, #203).
 *
 * COMPOSE: renders the sidebar, then the reveal script (`REVEAL_CURRENT_SCRIPT`,
 * `lib/route-shaping.ts`) that scrolls the sidebar pane so the current page's entry
 * is in view. On a site with no opt-in the sidebar is Starlight's own, unchanged:
 * nothing wraps it and nothing is added inside it. A site that opted in gets
 * `CustomSidebarBody`, which renders a DocKitty sublist in Starlight's persister
 * (ADR-0075, superseding ADR-0063 decision 1 in part).
 *
 * The manifest decides, and exports `CustomSidebarBody` only for such a site. A static
 * import here would put the body's scoped CSS in every site's module graph, opted in or
 * not. `Body` is rebound rather than branched on, so the whitespace Astro emits around
 * this element, and with it a stock site's bytes, stays what it was.
 *
 * Why here and not in `<head>`: a head script cannot reach the pane until the
 * document is parsed, so it had to wait for `DOMContentLoaded`, and on a slow
 * connection the sidebar was painted at the top and then jumped. Rendered after
 * the default, the script follows the whole sidebar in source order, so when
 * the parser runs it the pane and its `aria-current` entry exist and Starlight's
 * in-session scroll restore (the inline script at the end of
 * `<sl-sidebar-state-persist>`, inside the default) has already run. The reveal
 * moves the pane only when the entry is outside its visible part, so a restored
 * position wins. It runs before the sidebar is first painted.
 *
 * The script is classic and inline (`is:inline`: no `type=module`, no `defer`,
 * no `async`), so it runs as soon as it is parsed. `aria-hidden="true"` follows
 * Starlight's own sidebar scripts, which carry it for a Safari/VoiceOver bug that
 * reads out scripts inside a `display: contents` container. `data-dk-sidebar-reveal`
 * marks it for `assert-chrome-artifacts.mjs`.
 *
 * Starlight renders this override as `<Sidebar />` with no props and no
 * children; both bodies read `Astro.locals.starlightRoute`. `Astro.props` and
 * the slot are still forwarded, so a later Starlight that passes either reaches
 * the default unchanged.
 */
import Default from '@astrojs/starlight/components/Sidebar.astro';
import { CustomSidebarBody } from 'virtual:doc-kitty/manifest';
import { REVEAL_CURRENT_SCRIPT } from '../lib/route-shaping.js';

const Body = CustomSidebarBody ?? Default;
---
<Body {...Astro.props}><slot /></Body>
<script is:inline aria-hidden="true" data-dk-sidebar-reveal set:html={REVEAL_CURRENT_SCRIPT} />
